00:00:30.512 --> 00:00:32.485
- Given what I usually
eat, what I've been eating

00:00:32.485 --> 00:00:34.645
the last few days has been miraculous.

00:00:34.645 --> 00:00:37.733
- My meals tend to
usually be pretty healthy,

00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:40.225
but everything in between
is absolutely terrible.

00:00:44.865 --> 00:00:46.652
- So this is all I'm gonna eat today.

00:00:46.652 --> 00:00:47.785
- They've all got numbers on 'em,

00:00:47.785 --> 00:00:49.085
so I'm not gonna screw 'em up.

00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:50.757
- Like I like juice a lot, so I think

00:00:50.757 --> 00:00:52.220
I'm gonna enjoy drinking them.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.031
- What happens if I just drink all of them

00:00:54.031 --> 00:00:55.470
in the next 20 minutes?

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.442
- I think it's gonna be
an adventure of sorts.

00:00:58.912 --> 00:01:00.231
- All I want is like

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:01.962
to get a sandwich.

00:01:03.056 --> 00:01:06.192
Just a sandwich. It's sad
how good that would be.

00:01:06.192 --> 00:01:08.580
- I have a serious aversion to cilantro.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:11.673
It starts to hurt my.

00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:14.483
- [Garrett] And that's
what they're eating.

00:01:16.063 --> 00:01:17.221
And this is what I have.

00:01:17.221 --> 00:01:18.753
- You like that one?

00:01:18.753 --> 00:01:19.937
- I haven't tried that one yet.

00:01:19.937 --> 00:01:21.168
- You don't like beets though, right?

00:01:21.168 --> 00:01:22.700
- No, I think beets taste like dirt.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.561
- [Jordan] I like the first three.

00:01:24.561 --> 00:01:26.590
- [Garrett] The best one
by far is number three

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.242
which is called liquid gold.

00:01:28.242 --> 00:01:30.144
And it is delicious.

00:01:30.144 --> 00:01:31.509
- I like the spicy one the best.

00:01:31.509 --> 00:01:32.252
That's my jam.

00:01:32.252 --> 00:01:33.715
- [Garrett] The last
three juices of the day

00:01:33.715 --> 00:01:36.455
had like two pounds of produce in them,

00:01:36.455 --> 00:01:37.825
so they're much harder to drink.

00:01:37.825 --> 00:01:41.593
- The reason most people
drink like vegetably juices

00:01:41.593 --> 00:01:43.961
I think is not for
flavor, but is for the way

00:01:43.961 --> 00:01:45.261
that it makes you feel.

00:01:47.697 --> 00:01:49.954
- Yesterday, there were
times when I was just like

00:01:49.954 --> 00:01:52.010
I could just eat; I could
just go to the McDonald's

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.750
across the street and
just be done with this,

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.049
but now I've sort of
pushed through the phase

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:59.487
and I'll be like no, I can handle this.

00:01:59.887 --> 00:02:01.929
- I'm walking around the
office to get my juice

00:02:01.929 --> 00:02:03.972
and we have free lunch today.

00:02:04.522 --> 00:02:07.984
There's still all these
sandwiches that look super good,

00:02:07.984 --> 00:02:09.912
and I just have to eat stupid juice.

00:02:09.912 --> 00:02:12.373
- I've heard that kind of between
your first and second day,

00:02:12.373 --> 00:02:15.229
you hit like a fatigue stage
and I think I'm still at that.

00:02:15.229 --> 00:02:18.038
- It's a really weird
feeling to not be hungry,

00:02:18.038 --> 00:02:19.873
but to want food very badly.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:22.102
- I didn't realize how
much of my daily happiness

00:02:22.102 --> 00:02:23.286
food gave me.

00:02:25.426 --> 00:02:26.963
To get me through the juice cleanse,

00:02:26.963 --> 00:02:31.236
I wanted to have a physical
representation of my progress.

00:02:31.236 --> 00:02:33.952
That's all the food that
I've had the last three days.

00:02:33.952 --> 00:02:36.739
- I've just hit like a level of apathy

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:38.062
about the whole thing.

00:02:38.062 --> 00:02:39.306
- I'm feeling fine.

00:02:39.306 --> 00:02:42.301
Like I feel, I wake up in
the mornings and just like

00:02:42.301 --> 00:02:44.507
oh, well I guess I drink juice today.

00:02:44.507 --> 00:02:46.388
- I just had a lot of
trouble focusing yesterday.

00:02:46.388 --> 00:02:48.620
My brain was pretty foggy
until late in the afternoon.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:53.171
- It's hard to articulate
the kind of fatigue I feel.

00:02:53.171 --> 00:02:55.144
- I'm ready for it to be over,

00:02:55.144 --> 00:02:58.255
but I'm not dying to eat either.

00:03:00.395 --> 00:03:02.179
- I made it. I survived.

00:03:02.179 --> 00:03:04.152
- I'm still just kinda
tired and don't feel

00:03:04.152 --> 00:03:07.867
